WEBVTT

00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:50.566
No...

00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:53.566
Be more gentle...

00:01:59.066 --> 00:02:01.296
Those are my thighs.

00:02:06.866 --> 00:02:08.796
Alright, you done copying?

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:09.803
Yes.

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:12.396
Alright, Bouquet. Now page two.

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:14.066
We'll keep going?

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.800
I've been doing this the whole time,
you know!

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.370
We can take a break soon.
Let's hang in there, Boss Lady.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.570
Okay, okay, fine.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:29.803
Hipopon, Hipotama, Transform!
Turn into the second page!

00:02:31.266 --> 00:02:34.126
Flap-flap, do with us as you will.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.970
Kluke, please copy it.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:38.870
Right.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.600
Marumaro...

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.700
Maro?

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.533
You and I got time on our hands...

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.100
Yeah, we sure do, maro...

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.330
I know we can't increase
our Shadows' power

00:02:59.366 --> 00:03:01.966
until we translate
the Extra Seven, but...

00:03:02.066 --> 00:03:04.466
We can't read ancient letters
like that, maro.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.230
You guys sure have it easy.

00:03:07.566 --> 00:03:11.096
Announce yourselves as useless
and you don't have to do anything.

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.533
I don't have the energy
to bite back, maro.

00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:19.073
We're not being useless because we like it.
The least we can do is not get in the way.

00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:28.266
THE EXTRA SEVEN

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.373
Good work, Bouquet.

00:03:32.766 --> 00:03:35.266
Oh, I'm exhausted!

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.233
Umm, do you understand it?

00:03:43.566 --> 00:03:47.896
More or less.
But it seems it's not that simple.

00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:49.903
What do you mean?

00:03:50.466 --> 00:03:55.096
Looking at the whole thing, you can tell
this text is broken up into eight sections.

00:03:55.733 --> 00:04:00.233
And at a glance, the first section
appears to be a prose poem.

00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:01.873
A poem?

00:04:01.966 --> 00:04:02.626
Yes.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:06.103
But the second half of it is
a long string of meaningless text.

00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:07.733
It's an anagram.

00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:10.366
Reading this ancient language
is tough enough.

00:04:10.966 --> 00:04:13.026
And it's written in anagrams
on top of that.

00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:14.766
This sure is a tough one.

00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:19.233
We don't have the time to be whining.
Anyway, I'll give it a try.

00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:28.626
Hey, Jiro. What's this "ana" thing?

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.603
You don't even know that?

00:04:32.266 --> 00:04:34.426
To put it simply, it's a secret code.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:39.503
You rearrange the letters or
replace letters with numbers.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.430
You determine rules beforehand so others
can't understand it even if they see it.

00:04:45.433 --> 00:04:50.873
I don't really get it, maro.
Why do something so complicated?

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Well, it wouldn't be much
of a code if it were easy!

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.103
But there's no point if we
can't understand it, maro.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.673
Zola's working hard deciphering it
so that doesn't happen.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.200
I'm not really big on puzzles,
wire puzzles and stuff like that...

00:05:04.566 --> 00:05:07.896
Zola's doing something
a thousand times more complicated.

00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:09.533
Just watch quietly.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:12.670
Maro?

00:05:12.733 --> 00:05:13.873
W-What is it?!

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.430
You're watching quietly, too.
Does that mean you're useless too, maro?

00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:26.073
Oh, come on.
You should've told us that sooner, Jiro.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.000
Sh-Shut up!
Don't lump me in with you guys!

00:05:29.633 --> 00:05:34.633
You don't need to worry about it, maro!
We're "no-good comrades," maro!

00:05:35.466 --> 00:05:38.596
Now, now, Jiro. We're all useless.

00:05:38.633 --> 00:05:43.333
Listen! I'm telling you!
Don't lump me in with you guys!

00:05:43.366 --> 00:05:44.426
Oh, come on.

00:05:44.466 --> 00:05:46.766
Are you upset because
you've been told the truth?!

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.830
Say what?!

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.603
Knock it off!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.070
Be quiet, guys!
Let's all just watch quietly.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.500
- Okay...
- Okay, maro...

00:06:10.166 --> 00:06:13.966
The basic elements to compose words
are combinations of vowels and consonants.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.730
Naturally, more frequently-used letters
will become self-evident.

00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:23.433
I can guess the rules of this anagrams
by applying other ancient language systems

00:06:23.466 --> 00:06:28.066
and from the arrangement
of the poem in the first half.

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:33.873
Then if I factor in that pattern of
composition and start applying...

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.400
Done.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.500
Did you figure it out?!

00:06:56.633 --> 00:06:58.303
What does it say, maro?!

00:07:00.066 --> 00:07:01.226
Calm down.

00:07:04.233 --> 00:07:06.573
Okay, I'm going to read
the text I deciphered.

00:07:08.233 --> 00:07:09.233
Prologue...

00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:13.603
Excessive power begets
new misfortune.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:19.873
The Soldiers of Light vanished
from history after all battles ended.

00:07:20.733 --> 00:07:23.533
The soldiers returned
to their homelands and

00:07:24.433 --> 00:07:29.473
bid farewell to their Shadow companions
in their own ways.

00:07:31.766 --> 00:07:32.426
That's all.

00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:36.466
So then the Shadows were sealed?

00:07:36.766 --> 00:07:39.726
Meaning your theory
was right after all, Zola.

00:07:41.366 --> 00:07:44.596
However, this is just
the prologue of the Extra Seven.

00:07:45.066 --> 00:07:48.066
The text is broken up into eight sections,
which means...

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:52.730
The way to seal everyone's Shadows
is written in the remaining seven sections!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.900
It's too soon to rest easy.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.530
Further analysis is necessary,

00:07:58.766 --> 00:08:04.266
but I wasn't able to decipher the other texts
using the same anagram analysis.

00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:08.533
In other words, each section has
its own mystery to be solved.

00:08:09.466 --> 00:08:12.566
That's right.
We've made a good start.

00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:18.203
From here on, we will decipher each text
and carry out further analysis. Okay?

00:08:18.533 --> 00:08:19.203
- Right!
- Right!

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:35.733
General Logi of the Third Independent
Flying Squadron at your service.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.970
At ease.

00:08:38.066 --> 00:08:39.726
At ease! At ease!

00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:45.103
It seems you were defeated
rather spectacularly, Logi.

00:08:46.366 --> 00:08:48.126
How was Zola?

00:08:48.466 --> 00:08:49.126
Fine, sir.

00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:55.433
I lost two flying squadron officers
because of her.

00:09:00.766 --> 00:09:05.096
Of all people,
you who used to bathe in your glory...

00:09:05.266 --> 00:09:09.796
You sure have fallen.
You're just a shadow of your former self.

00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:12.903
Szabo, that's enough.

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:14.703
Logi...

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.070
Yes, sir?

00:09:16.866 --> 00:09:21.426
Those kids...
I take it that they have gotten stronger?

00:09:21.833 --> 00:09:27.633
The Power Booster I submitted
to you was just a prototype,

00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:32.896
but it could increase the power
of Shadows by several folds.

00:09:33.466 --> 00:09:35.426
We used it during our battle
yet the results are as you know.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:37.570
I see...

00:09:38.766 --> 00:09:39.996
Is that okay?

00:09:40.466 --> 00:09:43.566
If you don't punish him,
you'll set a bad example for the entire army.

00:09:44.566 --> 00:09:45.996
You have a point.

00:09:49.966 --> 00:09:52.596
Logi. Take a break for a while.

00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:59.673
And think about what you should do.
Think about your future.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.170
Yes, sir.

00:10:04.533 --> 00:10:05.633
General Logi.

00:10:05.966 --> 00:10:08.826
Your failure in the last operation
has affected

00:10:08.866 --> 00:10:11.266
the morale of
the entire Grankingdom Army.

00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:13.933
You bear great responsibility for that

00:10:13.966 --> 00:10:17.096
and you will be dismissed as commander
of the Third Independent Flying Squadron.

00:10:17.533 --> 00:10:21.403
You will be dispatched to a remote
garrison force on the mainland.

00:10:21.633 --> 00:10:23.033
I'm being relegated, huh?

00:10:23.466 --> 00:10:26.626
Well, it'll be easier for me
to work that way.

00:10:28.566 --> 00:10:31.466
Your day is done, Logi!

00:11:49.333 --> 00:11:51.473
Boobs...

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:53.670
- Ow!
- Boobs...

00:11:54.666 --> 00:11:55.766
Jeez...

00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:16.166
Oh, it's you, Shu.

00:12:17.466 --> 00:12:18.126
How's it going?

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:22.030
Just what I'd expect
of the Extra Seven...

00:12:24.833 --> 00:12:27.633
I mean that this puzzle
isn't easily solved.

00:12:28.433 --> 00:12:29.433
I see.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:31.270
What is it?

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.800
Oh, I was just thinking that
you're admirable, Zola.

00:12:38.233 --> 00:12:41.303
I'm just doing what I believe in.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.830
It's not something other people
have business commenting about.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:46.900
Well, that's true, but...

00:12:48.233 --> 00:12:50.473
Isn't that the same with you, too?

00:12:57.666 --> 00:12:59.766
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:05.630
Then we don't have time to waste.
Wake everyone up.

00:13:06.666 --> 00:13:09.126
From here on,
I'm going to need everyone's help.

00:13:09.766 --> 00:13:10.426
Right!

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:21.796
We're all here now.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:29.970
Are these copies of the Extra Seven?!

00:13:30.466 --> 00:13:32.826
It looks like they've been translated
into the current language...

00:13:33.466 --> 00:13:34.496
Chapter one.

00:13:34.566 --> 00:13:36.396
The soldier who protects the west,

00:13:36.433 --> 00:13:40.203
emerges from the forest with a quiet eye
behind him, and arrives at the land.

00:13:40.233 --> 00:13:42.673
A crimson light,
at the time of silence,

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:46.330
a new Shadow is born from the guardian
of the sky and shows the way...

00:13:46.933 --> 00:13:48.173
What is this?!

00:13:48.833 --> 00:13:51.773
This one sounds like
a fairy tale or something.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.200
This one is a long list of numbers.

00:13:54.466 --> 00:13:56.726
This one has pictures, maro.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:01.230
As you can see, it's the Extra Seven
translated into our language.

00:14:01.733 --> 00:14:06.603
While I translated, I also tried to
solve the puzzle, but I couldn't do it.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.330
One of these seven texts
contains information

00:14:10.366 --> 00:14:13.226
about the sealing of
your particular Shadow.

00:14:13.633 --> 00:14:14.633
Anything will do.

00:14:15.033 --> 00:14:20.603
Take a look at all of the texts and
let me know if you notice anything.

00:14:20.933 --> 00:14:22.073
But...

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:23.100
Maro...

00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:26.626
Will we be able to manage something
that even you can't figure out?

00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:33.003
Yes. Like I said, these texts contain
information about your own Shadow.

00:14:33.633 --> 00:14:38.803
There's a good chance that there's
something you guys will notice that I can't.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:40.300
We just have to do this!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.800
We won't be able to defeat Nene
unless we decipher these texts.

00:14:45.366 --> 00:14:46.026
- Right!
- Maro!

00:14:46.766 --> 00:14:49.696
Alright. Let's get to work.

00:14:50.133 --> 00:14:52.133
Th-Then I'm off to do some shopping!

00:14:53.866 --> 00:14:56.426
You'll decipher this text with me.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.730
So heavy...

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:05.296
Man, they asked for so many things
because they aren't the ones carrying them.

00:15:06.133 --> 00:15:09.973
Now, now. Everyone's doing their best,
so don't complain.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.170
I know, but...

00:15:13.666 --> 00:15:14.326
But...

00:15:16.566 --> 00:15:18.266
How about we take a little detour?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.570
Being stuck all day inside
a library with poor ventilation

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.900
kind of makes you feel depressed,
doesn't it?!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.830
That's true.

00:15:36.933 --> 00:15:41.203
An ordinary sight like this looks
like something very important now...

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.500
It's weird, isn't it?

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:48.300
I never thought things would turn out
like this just a little while ago.

00:15:50.333 --> 00:15:51.833
It all started back at that time.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.430
I wanted to protect
everyone then...

00:15:59.566 --> 00:16:00.296
But...

00:16:03.133 --> 00:16:04.633
But, I...

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.930
Shu, look at that.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.670
Hey, come on!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.870
Hurry!

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:16.900
Okay, stay right there!

00:16:19.933 --> 00:16:24.033
We played like that back in
Talta Village, didn't we?

00:16:24.666 --> 00:16:25.326
Yeah.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:29.300
I did nothing but
stupid things back then.

00:16:30.766 --> 00:16:33.066
Running around
the forest like a goofball...

00:16:37.966 --> 00:16:39.526
Building our secret fort...

00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:44.973
Getting all muddy in puddles of water
like bunch of idiots...

00:16:45.966 --> 00:16:47.596
And sneaking into ruins...

00:16:51.333 --> 00:16:52.333
What is it?

00:16:52.866 --> 00:16:53.996
I remember.

00:16:54.033 --> 00:16:57.533
There was one time we all went exploring
and you got separated from the rest of us.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:58.570
Oh!

00:16:59.633 --> 00:17:01.733
That was the worst...

00:17:04.733 --> 00:17:07.133
- I fell down into a pit...
- Ow!

00:17:07.166 --> 00:17:11.266
I ripped the hem of my favorite clothes
and my wallet string broke...

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.100
I lost my way.
It was dark and I got scared.

00:17:15.333 --> 00:17:19.303
It felt like a monster would appear or
like I was being watched by someone...

00:17:21.033 --> 00:17:22.033
Someone?

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.670
What is it?

00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:31.326
Oh!

00:17:32.066 --> 00:17:33.396
What is it?

00:17:37.666 --> 00:17:40.396
This is it! Let's go, Shu!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.030
Oh, hey!

00:17:42.466 --> 00:17:43.466
Kluke!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.500
Hey! Wait up, Kluke!

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.930
What the hell's going on?

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.270
I figured it out!

00:17:54.966 --> 00:17:55.626
Huh?

00:17:56.266 --> 00:17:57.796
Just hurry up!

00:17:57.833 --> 00:18:01.473
Hurry? But, hey!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:04.570
You carry some of this, too!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.300
I'm hungry, maro.

00:18:07.966 --> 00:18:09.726
Me, too.

00:18:13.033 --> 00:18:14.033
What is it?

00:18:14.166 --> 00:18:16.196
I figured out the meaning of the text!

00:18:16.833 --> 00:18:17.503
What?!

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:22.703
The food's here, maro!

00:18:26.466 --> 00:18:28.026
Sorry, but food has to wait.

00:18:28.633 --> 00:18:30.203
- What?!
- What?!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.270
Kluke, please explain.

00:18:33.466 --> 00:18:35.766
Sure!
It's about this text.

00:18:36.266 --> 00:18:37.366
Chapter one?

00:18:38.933 --> 00:18:40.403
The soldier who protects the west,

00:18:40.433 --> 00:18:44.733
emerges from the forest with a quiet eye
behind him, and arrives at the land.

00:18:44.933 --> 00:18:47.533
A crimson light, at the time of silence,

00:18:47.566 --> 00:18:51.266
a new Shadow is born from the guardian
of the sky, and shows the way.

00:18:51.666 --> 00:18:57.066
The soldier lost in darkness,
finds the answer between truth and lies...

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.500
This is probably talking about
the ruins in Talta Village!

00:19:00.766 --> 00:19:01.426
What?!

00:19:01.966 --> 00:19:02.996
Please explain.

00:19:03.633 --> 00:19:07.503
The soldier who protects the west,
a quiet eye, forest...

00:19:07.933 --> 00:19:11.333
I think all three of them
are in the ruins in Talta.

00:19:11.733 --> 00:19:14.703
What do you mean?
I can understand a forest being there, but...

00:19:14.733 --> 00:19:17.533
There's a soldier and
an eye in the ruins, maro?

00:19:17.566 --> 00:19:20.966
Yes. Those two are in
the form of a relief, though.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.270
- A relief?
- A relief?

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:26.030
I got lost in the ruins long time ago
and saw them.

00:19:28.466 --> 00:19:31.996
On the west side of those ruins,
there was the relief of a soldier,

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:36.000
and next to that was
a relief of a strange eye...

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:40.200
This is just my guess,

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:46.670
but there just might be something with
a picture of a forest beyond that point...

00:19:48.533 --> 00:19:52.773
In other words, I think this text
is referring to the ruins in Talta.

00:19:56.766 --> 00:19:57.766
I see.

00:19:58.533 --> 00:20:01.033
That's awesome, Kluke! And?

00:20:01.933 --> 00:20:02.603
Huh?

00:20:02.933 --> 00:20:05.003
What's the rest of the text
suppose to mean?

00:20:05.166 --> 00:20:07.866
I... I don't know that either.

00:20:07.933 --> 00:20:11.903
Come on. That's the same
as not knowing anything at all.

00:20:11.966 --> 00:20:12.966
What did you say?!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.700
No, that's wrong.

00:20:14.933 --> 00:20:15.603
- What?!
- What?!

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:20.200
It's been explained that one of the texts
is about the ruins in Talta.

00:20:20.733 --> 00:20:22.073
This is significant progress.

00:20:25.466 --> 00:20:27.566
Let's go. To the ruins in Talta!

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.600
But how do we get there?!

00:20:29.933 --> 00:20:32.133
It's quite a long way to the ruins...

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:33.700
Yeah...

00:20:37.466 --> 00:20:40.496
It's an enemy attack!
Mobilize the Robot Soldiers!

00:21:00.533 --> 00:21:01.203
All right!

00:21:01.433 --> 00:21:02.733
Don't take it too far!

00:21:03.033 --> 00:21:05.573
We should just take it easy
on enemies like these!

00:21:06.066 --> 00:21:07.196
I know!

00:21:07.466 --> 00:21:09.366
Oh, look at that, maro!

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:20.200
They're trying to run away!

00:21:20.233 --> 00:21:21.833
I don't think so!

00:21:33.433 --> 00:21:34.433
All right!

00:21:34.466 --> 00:21:35.126
Very good!

00:21:48.833 --> 00:21:49.503
That one looks good!

00:21:57.966 --> 00:21:58.626
How's it look?!

00:21:58.866 --> 00:21:59.526
It should be fine!

00:22:02.966 --> 00:22:03.996
What's the plan?!

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:05.570
Just blast through!

00:22:06.166 --> 00:22:06.826
Roger!

00:22:18.166 --> 00:22:18.826
Here they come!

00:22:19.566 --> 00:22:21.366
Jump in, everyone!

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:22.870
- Got it!
- Got it!

00:22:29.633 --> 00:22:30.673
Alright! Nice.

00:22:33.366 --> 00:22:36.096
Alright, let's head for
the ruins in Talta Village.

00:22:36.233 --> 00:22:36.903
Roger.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:39.900
Now we can hop around
to anywhere in the world.

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:41.100
Maro.

00:24:18.333 --> 00:24:20.633
Shu has come to the ruins
in order to power up.

00:24:20.666 --> 00:24:22.796
There he meets the dark Blue Dragon.

00:24:22.833 --> 00:24:25.533
Is this my new Blue Dragon?

00:24:25.566 --> 00:24:27.926
Huh?! How did you
come to that conclusion?

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:29.466
You know, when you talk
about powering up,

00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.600
you usually upgrade
to something new.

00:24:30.633 --> 00:24:32.973
I thought it was about time for a change.

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.400
You two-timer!

00:24:34.433 --> 00:24:36.803
Next on Blue Dragon:
The Dark Dragon
